# Keep shell and Python scripts LF on every platform.  Without this,
# Windows checkouts (core.autocrlf) inject CRLF, and bash chokes on the
# trailing \r ($'\r': command not found) when the script is later run in
# a Linux / qemu container.  This is exactly what broke tests/obfstr in
# the WSL test run.
*.sh  text eol=lf
*.py  text eol=lf
